.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt SCHEDULER 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm scheduler
.Nd common scheduler controls and statistics
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
interface provides sysctls shared by the system schedulers.
Scheduler-specific controls are described in
.Xr sched_4bsd 4
and
.Xr sched_ule 4 .
.Pp
The following sysctls are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va kern.sched.name
The name of the active scheduler.
This is read-only at run time, but can be set as a boot-time tunable to select
a scheduler compiled into the kernel.
.It Va kern.sched.available
A comma-separated list of schedulers compiled into the kernel.
.It Va kern.sched.preemption
Whether kernel preemption support was compiled in.
This value is read-only and cannot be changed at run time.
.It Va kern.sched.cpusetsize
The size, in bytes, of the kernel's
.Vt cpuset_t .
.It Va kern.sched.cpusetsizemin
The minimum supported size, in bytes, of a CPU set passed to the kernel.
.It Va kern.sched.topology_spec
An XML description of the detected CPU topology.
See
.Xr smp 4
for the format.
.El
.Pp
When the kernel is built with
.Cd "options SCHED_STATS" ,
the following sysctls are also available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va kern.sched.stats
A node containing read-only counters for scheduling events.
These include context-switch reasons and interrupt-thread events;
additional counters depend on the scheduler.
.It Va kern.sched.stats.reset
Writing a nonzero value resets the scheduler statistics to zero.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sched_4bsd 4 ,
.Xr sched_ule 4 ,
.Xr smp 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
